# G104 — Report Generator

*v2. See `report-generator.md` for prose: kind-tagged rows (Header/
Data/Subtotal/Total), declarative column specs, grouped subtotals
emitted alongside their data, per-column cents formatting.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Sales Dashboard

[vault-sales-dashboard @year
    IN ORDER TO
        pull this year's orders into a grouped report
        render it in the dashboard with kind-aware styling
        and export the same data as tab-delimited text on demand

    @records <- [vault[query {table: "orders", year: @year}]]

    @spec <- [report[spec
        {title: "Sales by Region — " + @year,
         columns: [
            {name: "Region",  field: "region",  kind: "plain"}
            {name: "Product", field: "product", kind: "plain"}
            {name: "Qty",     field: "qty",     kind: "sum_aggregate"}
            {name: "Revenue", field: "revenue", kind: "sum_aggregate",
                              format-cents: true}
         ],
         group-by: "region"}]]

    @report <- [report[generate {records: @records, spec: @spec}]]

    [ui[render-report {report: @report}]]

    sync @user-events {
        export-csv ->
            [vault[save {path: "exports/sales-" + @year + ".txt",
                          content: [report[render {report: @report}]]}]]
    }
]

---

## Verb Surface

[report
    spec             {title, columns, group-by}
    generate         {records, spec}
    render           {report}                     ;; -> String (tab-delimited)
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: row kind as `where` dispatch key

[@report:rows
    where kind is Header      -> [ui[render-header {cells: @row:cells}]]
    where kind is Data        -> [ui[render-data   {cells: @row:cells}]]
    where kind is Subtotal    -> [ui[render-subtotal
                                       {cells: @row:cells,
                                        group: @row:group-label}]]
    where kind is Total       -> [ui[render-total  {cells: @row:cells}]]
]

Rather than the consumer inferring row semantics from position (fragile
when subtotals nest or totals repeat in multi-level reports), every
row carries its kind. The `where` clauses are the dispatch table.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: aggregate exists `where` column is summable

[report[generate {records: @r, spec: @s}]
    IN ORDER TO
        emit data rows interleaved with subtotals
        and append a grand total
        where any column in @s:columns has kind sum_aggregate
        (otherwise the Total row is omitted)
]

Grand total existence is a constraint on the spec, not a caller flag.
If nothing is summable, nothing meaningful can total — the report
ends at the last Data row.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @records <- [
        {region: "East", product: "Widget", qty: 3, revenue: 1500}
        {region: "East", product: "Gadget", qty: 2, revenue: 2000}
        {region: "West", product: "Widget", qty: 5, revenue: 2500}
        {region: "West", product: "Gizmo",  qty: 1, revenue: 750}
    ]

    @spec <- [report[spec
        {title: "Sales Report",
         columns: [
            {name: "Region",  field: "region",  kind: "plain"}
            {name: "Product", field: "product", kind: "plain"}
            {name: "Qty",     field: "qty",     kind: "sum_aggregate"}
            {name: "Revenue", field: "revenue", kind: "sum_aggregate",
                              format-cents: true}
         ],
         group-by: "region"}]]

    -> [report[render {report: [report[generate {records: @records,
                                                   spec: @spec}]]}]]
    ;; Sales Report
    ;; # Region  Product  Qty  Revenue
    ;;   East    Widget   3    $15.00
    ;;   East    Gadget   2    $20.00
    ;; ~ East subtotal    5    $35.00
    ;;   West    Widget   5    $25.00
    ;;   West    Gizmo    1    $7.50
    ;; ~ West subtotal    6    $32.50
    ;; = TOTAL            11   $67.50
]
